      }
    ],
    "pathway_role_summary": "CTNNB1 is the central effector of canonical Wnt signaling. In the absence of Wnt ligand, it is phosphorylated by GSK3B/CK1 in the destruction complex (with APC and AXIN) and degraded via beta-TrCP-mediated ubiquitination. Upon Wnt stimulation, the destruction complex is inhibited, beta-catenin stabilizes and translocates to the nucleus where it binds TCF/LEF transcription factors and coactivators (BCL9, CBP/p300) to activate Wnt target genes controlling proliferation, differentiation, and stem cell maintenance. CTNNB1 also has a structural role in cell adhesion as part of the cadherin-catenin complex at adherens junctions."
  },
